  "result": "Perfect! All 48 tests pass. Here's what I added:\n\n**addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })** \u2014 Modifies a draft invoice by adding or incrementing a line:\n- Validates invoice is in draft status with a proper lines array\n- Validates qty is a positive integer and SKU exists in the catalogue (same errors as `createInvoice`)\n- If the SKU already exists on the invoice, increases its qty\n- Otherwise, appends a new line with enriched product data\n- Never mutates the original invoice\n\n**removeLine(invoice, sku)** \u2014 Removes a line from a draft invoice:\n- Validates invoice is in draft status with a proper lines array\n- Returns `fail('LINE_NOT_FOUND')` if the SKU isn't on the invoice\n- Returns `fail('NO_LINES')` if removing it would be the last line\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with the line removed\n- Never mutates the original invoice\n\n**Error codes added:**\n- `NOT_DRAFT` \u2014 invoice must be in draft status to modify\n- `LINE_NOT_FOUND` \u2014 SKU not found on the invoice\n\n**Tests** \u2014 14 new test cases covering:\n- Adding new lines and incrementing existing ones\n- Validation of qty and SKU\n- Immutability\n- Non-draft invoice protection\n- Line removal with edge cases",
